      "speaker": "Representative of Iran",
      "role": "Delegate to the Third Committee",
      "affiliation": "Iran",
      "iso2": "IR",
      "date": "2026-10-02",
      "venue": "other",
      "quote": "International humanitarian law does not become optional because the perpetrator sits on the Security Council,",
      "paraphrase": "Iran's representative rejected the use of human rights as coercion, said the Third Committee should not launder crimes of hegemonic powers, and accused the United States and Israel of killing 168 children and teachers in a 28 February strike on a school in Minab, arguing international humanitarian law applies even to Security Council members and that silence and selective outrage amount to complicity.",
